Here's a PHP code that calculates the net present value (NPV) of the investment:
```
$revenue_growth_rate = 0.10;
$profit_margin = 0.15;
$debt_to_equity_ratio = 0.5;
$initial_investment = -10000000;
$annual_revenue = 5000000;
$years = 5;
$cost_of_capital = 0.10;
$free_cash_flow = array();
$discount_factor = array();
for ($i = 1; $i <= $years; $i++) {
    $free_cash_flow[$i] = ($annual_revenue * pow((1 + $revenue_growth_rate), $i)) * $profit_margin * (1 - $debt_to_equity_ratio) - ($initial_investment / $years);
    $discount_factor[$i] = 1 / pow((1 + $cost_of_capital), $i);
}
$npv = array_sum(array_map(function($a, $b) { return $a * $b; }, $free_cash_flow, $discount_factor));
echo "The net present value of the investment is $" . number_format($npv, 2) . ".";
if ($npv > 0) {
    echo " The company should invest in the new product line.";
} else {
    echo " The company should not invest in the new product line.";
}
```
