Here's an example of how sentiment analysis can be employed in MATLAB to analyze a corpus of text for expressions of comprehension:
```matlab
% Load the text data
textData = readtable('textData.csv');
% Clean the text data
cleanText = preprocessText(textData.Text);
% Perform sentiment analysis using the Text Analytics Toolbox
documents = tokenizedDocument(cleanText);
bag = bagOfWords(documents);
model = trainDocumentClassifier(bag, textData.Sentiment);
[labels, scores] = classify(model, bag);
% Analyze expressions of comprehension
comprehensionExpressions = ["I understand", "I get it", "It makes sense", "I comprehend"];
comprehensionIndices = contains(cleanText, comprehensionExpressions, 'IgnoreCase', true);
comprehensionSentiments = labels(comprehensionIndices);
comprehensionScores = scores(comprehensionIndices, :);
positiveComprehensionIndices = strcmp(comprehensionSentiments, 'Positive');
negativeComprehensionIndices = strcmp(comprehensionSentiments, 'Negative');
neutralComprehensionIndices = strcmp(comprehensionSentiments, 'Neutral');
positiveComprehensionScore = mean(comprehensionScores(positiveComprehensionIndices, 2));
negativeComprehensionScore = mean(comprehensionScores(negativeComprehensionIndices, 2));
neutralComprehensionScore = mean(comprehensionScores(neutralComprehensionIndices, 2));
% Display the results
