To generate an HTML page that summarizes the research article "The Effects of Social Media on Education" using PHP code, you will need to first retrieve the relevant information from the article. 
One way to do this is to use a web scraping tool like BeautifulSoup to extract the information from the article's webpage. Once you have extracted the information, you can use PHP to format and display it in an HTML page.
Here is an example PHP code that retrieves and displays the summary, methods, results, and conclusion from the article:
```php
<?php
    // Retrieve the webpage using cURL
    $url = "https://www.example.com/the-effects-of-social-media-on-education";
    $ch = curl_init();
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_URL, $url);
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, true);
    $html = curl_exec($ch);
    curl_close($ch);
    // Parse the HTML using BeautifulSoup
    $doc = new DOMDocument();
    @$doc->loadHTML($html);
    $xpath = new DOMXPath($doc);
    // Retrieve the relevant sections from the article
    $summary = $xpath->query('//div[@class="summary"]')->item(0)->nodeValue;
    $methods = $xpath->query('//div[@class="methods"]')->item(0)->nodeValue;
    $results = $xpath->query('//div[@class="results"]')->item(0)->nodeValue;
    $conclusion = $xpath->query('//div[@class="conclusion"]')->item(0)->nodeValue;
    // Display the sections in an HTML page
    echo '<html>
            <head>
                <title>The Effects of Social Media on Education</title>
            </head>
            <body>
                <h1>The Effects of Social Media on Education</h1>
                <h2>Summary</h2>
                <p>' . $summary . '</p>
                <h2>Methods</h2>
                <p>' . $methods . '</p>
                <h2>Results</h2>
                <p>' . $results . '</p>
                <h2>Conclusion</h2>
                <p>' . $conclusion . '</p>
            </body>
        </html>';
?>
